          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            is a combinatorial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model
            for a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            (an
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
          %p
            A
            %em simplicial group
            is a simplicial set with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            on it. It turns out that this necessarily means that it is also a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
                with an extra group structure on it;
            %li
              %p a model for a topological space with a group structure.
          %p
            Accordingly (as discussed at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            gives rise to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a one-object
                = succeed "-groupoid" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} G
                whose explicit standard realization as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                is denoted
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W G
            %li
              %p
                an
                = succeed "-groupoid" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi E
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E} G
                whose explicit standard realization as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                (even a simplicial group, again) is denoted
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G
            %li
              %p such that there is a fibration
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi E
                              %mi G
                            %mtd
                              %mo :
                              %mo =
                            %mtd
                              %mi W
                              %mi G
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mi G
                            %mtd
                              %mo :
                              %mo =
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mi W
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                              %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\mathbf{E} G
                      \&amp;:=&amp; W G
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      \\mathbf{B} G
                      \&amp;:=&amp;
                      \\bar W G
                      }
              %p
                which is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} universal G-bundle
          %p
            Simplicial abelian groups are models for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+spectrum"} connective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectrum"} modules
            over the
