          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            = succeed "," do
              %strong simplicial group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
            of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of simplicial groups is the category of functors from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{op}
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Simp
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Grp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Simp\Grp
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#AsKanComplexes As Kan complexes
          %p
          #EverySimplicialGroupIsAKanComplex.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              any simplicial group (by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetting
              the group
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          %p
            This is due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Moore54"} Moore 1954, Theorem 3 on p. 18-04
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Quillen67"} Quillen 67, II 3.8
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MaySimplicialObjects"} May 67, Theorem 17.1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Curtis71"} Curtis 1971, Sec. 3, Lem. 3.1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Weibel94"} Weibel 1994, Lem. 8.2.8
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#JoyalTierney05"} Joyal &amp; Tierney 2005, p. 14
          %p
            In fact, not only are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
            fillers guaranteed to exist, but there is an algorithm that provides explicit fillers. This implies that constructions on a simplicial group that use fillers of horns can often be adjusted to be functorial by using the algorithmically defined fillers. An argument that just uses ‘existence’ of fillers can be refined to give something more ‘coherent’.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a simplicial group.
            %p Here is the explicit algorithm that computes the horn fillers:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y_0,\ldots, y_{k-1}, -,y_{k+1}, \ldots, y_n)
              give a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{n-1}
              = succeed "s" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi y
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              simplices that fit together as if they were all but one, the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi th
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^{th}
              one, of the faces of an
              = succeed "-simplex." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
                %ul
                  %li
                    Let
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi w
                            %mi n
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mi y
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_n = s_{n-1}y_n
                    and then
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi w
                            %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi w
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi i
                          %msub
                            %mi w
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mi y
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_i = w_{i+1}(s_{i-1}d_i w_{i+1})^{-1}s_{i-1}y_i
