          .num_remark
            %h6#remarks Remarks
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The filler for any horn can be chosen to be a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %em product of degenerate elements
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+groups"} simplicial homotopy groups
                  of a simplicial group,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %li
                %p
                  A simplicial group can be considered as a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groupoid"} simplicial groupoid
                  having exactly one object. If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  is a simplicial group, the suggested notation for the corresponding simplicially enriched groupoid would be
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                  according to notational conventions suggested elsewhere in the nLab.
              %li
                %p
                  There is a functor due to Dwyer and Kan, called the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+loop+groupoid"} Dwyer-Kan loop groupoid
                  that takes a simplicial set to a simplicial groupoid. This has a left adjoint
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi W
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{W}
                  (see below), called the
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+classifying+space"} simplicial classifying space
                  functor, and together they give an equivalence of categories between the homotopy category of simplical sets and that of simplicial groupoids. We thus have that all homotopy types are modelled by simplicial groupoids … and for connected homotopy types by simplicial groups. One
                  %em important fact
                  to note in this equivalence is that it shifts dimension by 1, so if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(K)
                  is the simplicial group corresponding to the connected simplicial set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  then
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_k(K)
                  is the same as
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{k-1}(G(K))
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+n-type"} homotopy n-type
          %h3#FiberSequences Fiber sequences
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a simplicial group and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_0
              its group of 0-cells, regarded as a simplicially constant simplicial group. Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/G_0
              for the evident
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              of simplicial groups.
            %p The evident morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ≃
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G_0 \to G \to G/G_0 \simeq \mathbf{B} \Omega G/G_0
            %p
              form a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              One checks that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              any simplicial set and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a simplicial group acting freely on it, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \to X/G
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Weibel94"} Weibel, exercise 8.2.6
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
              it is therefore sufficient to observe that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi G
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi G
                              %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    G_0 &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    G &amp;\to&amp; G/G_0
                    }
            %p
              is an ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              of simplicial sets. This is clear since the action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_0
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is degreewise free (being the action of a subgroup).
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi δ
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G_1 \stackrel{\delta}{\to} G_0)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
              of groups, write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi δ
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi δ
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 0
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [G_1 \stackrel{\delta}{\to} G_0]
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    G_0 \times G_1
                    \\stackrel{\overset{(\delta p_2)\cdot p_1}{\to}}{\underset{p_1}{\to}}
                    G_0
                    \\right)
            %p
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              which is the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict 2-group
              and write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N[G_1 \to G_0]
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              being the corresponding simplicial group. Then the above says that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi δ
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G_0 \to [G_1 \stackrel{\delta}{\to} G_0]
                    \\to
                    \\mathbf{B}G_1
            %p
              is a fiber sequence of
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
          %h3#free_simplicial_groups Free simplicial groups
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} forgetful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi AbSGrpg
                    %mo →
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U : AbSGrpg \to SSet
            %p
              from simplicial
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo :
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi AbSimpGrp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{Z} : SSet \to AbSimpGrp
            %p
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              to abelian simplicial groups, the
              %strong free simplicial abelian group
              functor that sends the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n
              of
              = succeed "-simplices" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}X)_n = \mathbb{Z} X_n
              over it.
            %p
              This functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              has the following properties:
            %ul
              %li
                %p it preserves weak equivalences
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} X
                  is a cofibrant simplicial group
          %p (…)
          %h3#looping_and_delooping Looping and delooping
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ↪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_0 \hookrightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            be the category of
            %em reduced simplicial sets
            (simplicial sets with a single 0-cell).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in sSet_0
              define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sGrpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega X \in sGrpd
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 0
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega X :  [n] \mapsto  (F X_{n+1})/ s_0 F(X_n)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega X : ([n] \to [k]) \mapsto ...
          %h3#AsInfinityGroups
            As
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            Simplicial groups are models for
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+groups"} model structure on simplicial groups
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+(infinity%2C1)-category#ModelsInInfGrpd"} models for group objects in ∞Grpd
          %p
            Another equivalent model is that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          %p
            At the abstract level of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            this equivalence is induced by forming
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo :
                  %mn ∞
                  %msub
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mi con
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ←
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega
                  \:
                  \\infty Grpd_{con} \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to}
                  \\infty Grp
                  \:
                  \\mathbf{B}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+quasi-categories"} (∞,1)-equivalence
            is modeled by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            Quillen functor is the operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{W}
            discussed above.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mn 0
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Quillen
                  %mi sGrp
                  %mo :
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo ¯
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{G} : sSet_0 \stackrel{\stackrel{\simeq_{Quillen}}{\longleftarrow}}{\longrightarrow} sGrp
                  \: \overline{W}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is for instance in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine"} GoerssJardine, chapter 5
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+(infinity%2C1)-category#ModelsInInfGrpd"} group object in an (∞,1)-category – models for groups in ∞Grpd
          %h3#ClosedMonoidalStructure Closed monoidal structure
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sAb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sAb
            of simplicial abelian groups is naturally a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A,B]
            is the simplicial abelian group whose underlying simplicial set is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi sAb
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [A,B] : [n] \mapsto Hom_{sAb}(A \otimes \mathbb{Z}[\Delta[n]], B)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo →
                  %mi sAb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Z}[-] : sSet \to sAb
            is degreewise the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
            abelian group functor.
          %h2#DeloopingAndBundle Delooping and simplicial principal bundles
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a simplicial group, we describe its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G  \in sSet
            and the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}G \to \mathbf{B}G
            such that the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mo •
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi E
                          %mi G
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mo •
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P_\bullet &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{E}G
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X_\bullet &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                  }
          %p
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            models the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mo •
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mo •
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P_\bullet &amp;\to&amp; *
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X_\bullet &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            in the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            and hence produces the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_\bullet \to X_\bullet
            classified by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \to \mathbf{B}G
          %p For all these constructions exist very explicit combinatorial formulas that go by the symbols
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo ¯
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{W}G
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi E
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}G
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau : X_\bullet \to G_\bullet
                (called the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisting+function"} twisting function
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \to \mathbf{B}G
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi g
                      %mi W
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \times_g W G
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_\bullet
                (called
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cartesian+product"} twisted Cartesian product
                ).
          %p
            All of these constructions are functorial and hence lift from the context of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
            over some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} group objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            and
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, sSet]
            the pullback of the objectwise
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo ¯
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G \to \overline{W}G
            is still a homotopy pullback and models the corresponding principal
            = succeed "-bundles." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %h3#Delooping Delooping
          %p
            A simplicial group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} group object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to the category of
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            of that Kan complex reproduces
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            An explicit construction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            goes traditionally by the symbol
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi KanCplx
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W G \in KanCplx
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d B G
          %h4#delooping_modeled_by_
            Delooping modeled by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W G
          %p
            It is immediate to deloop the simplicial group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groupoid"} simplicial groupoid
            that in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is the 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            with a single object and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_k
            as its collection of morphisms.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groupoid"} simplicial groupoid
              that on objects is a constant simplicial set, define a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W \mathcal{G}
              as follows.
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mover
                          %mi W
                          %mo ¯
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 0
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mi ob
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\overline{W}\mathcal{G})_0 := ob(\mathcal{G}_0)
                  , the set of objects of the groupoid of 0-simplices (and hence of the groupoid at each level);
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mover
                          %mi W
                          %mo ¯
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 1
                        %mo =
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\overline{W}\mathcal{G})_1 = Mor(\mathcal{G}_0)
                  , the collection of
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒢
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_0
            %p
              and for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo ¯
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\overline{W}\mathcal{G})_n = \{(h_{n-1}, \ldots ,h_0)| h_i \in Mor(\mathcal{G}_i)
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi i
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(h_{i-1}) = t(h_i), 0\lt i\lt n\}
            %p
              Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              are generic symbols for the domain and codomain mappings of all the groupoids involved. The face and degeneracy mappings between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{W}(\mathcal{G})_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{W}(\mathcal{G})_0
              are the source and target maps and the identity maps of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_0
            %p The face and degeneracy maps are given by
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0(h_{n-1}, \ldots, h_0) = (h_{n-2}, \ldots, h_0)
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi i
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt  i\lt  n
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi …
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo −
                              %mn 2
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mi …
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mn 0
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mi i
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mi i
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mi i
                              %mo −
                              %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mi …
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_i(h_{n-1}, \ldots, h_0)  = (d_{i-1}h_{n-1}, d_{i-2}h_{n-2}, \ldots, d_0h_{n-i}h_{n-i-1},h_{n-i-2}, \ldots , h_0)
            %p and
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_n(h_{n-1}, \ldots, h_0) = (d_{n-1}h_{n-1}, d_{n-2}h_{n-2}, \ldots, d_1h_{1})
                ;
            %p whilst
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mrow
                          %mi dom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_0(h_{n-1}, \ldots, h_0) = (id_{dom(h_{n-1})},h_{n-1}, \ldots, h_0)
                ;
            %p and,
            %ul
              %li
                for
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi i
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\lt i \leq n
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mn 0
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mrow
                            %mi cod
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi h
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mi i
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_i(h_{n-1}, \ldots, h_0) = (s_{i-1}h_{n-1}, \ldots, s_0h_{n-i}, id_{cod(h_{n-i})},h_{n-i-1}, \ldots,  h_0)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a simplicial group and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
              the corresponding one-object
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groupoid"} simplicial groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\overline{W}G := \overline{W}\mathcal{G}
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The above construction has a straightforward
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalization
              to contexts other than
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
              in
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{W}G
              with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\overline{W}G)_n :=
                    G_{n-1} \times G_{n-2} \times \cdots \times G_0
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
              in this context (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"}> topological spaces
              ,
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %p
              In particular, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G : C^{op} \to sSet
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaf
              that is objectwise a simplicial group, then we have the simplicial presheaf
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mi c
                    %mo ↦
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\overline{W}G : c \mapsto \overline{W}(G(c))
                    \\,.
          %h4#delooping_modeled_by__2
            Delooping modeled by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d B G
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+set"} bisimplicial set
            obtained by taking degreewise the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d B G \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            for its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi d
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar W G \simeq d B G
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is shown for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#JardineLuo"}> JardineLuo
            ) and in (
            %a{:href => "#CegarraRemedios"}> CegarraRemedios
            ).
          %h4#examples Examples
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is an ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo ¯
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{W}G
            is the usual bar complex of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo ¯
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mo *
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\overline{W}G =
                  \\left(
                  \\cdots G \times G \stackrel{\to}{\stackrel{\to}{\to}} G \stackrel{\to}{\to} *
                  \\right)
                  \\,.
          %h3#UniversalBundle Cocycles
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo ¯
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g : X_\bullet \to \overline{W}G
          %p
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            corresponds precisely to what is called a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisting+function"} twisting function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{\phi(g)_n : X_n \to G_{n-1}\}
          %p satisfying the relations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mn 0
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mn 1
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mn 0
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi i
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi i
                          %mo &gt;
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi i
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi i
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mn 0
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi G
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  d_0 \phi(x) = \phi(d_1 x)(\phi(d_0 x))^{-1}
                  \\\
                  d_i \phi(x) = \phi(d_{i+1}x), i\gt 0,
                  \\\
                  s_i\phi(x) = \phi(s_{i+1}x), i\geq 0,
                  \\\
                  \\phi(s_0 x) = 1_G.
                  }
          %h3#PrincipalBundles Simplicial Principal bundles
          %p
            Simplicial groups model all
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            should be modeled by
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+principal+bundle"} simplicial principal bundle
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %strong (principal action)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a simplicial group. For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho : E \times G \to E
            %p
              is called
              %strong principal
              if it is degreewise principal, i.e. if for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              the only elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G_n
              that have any fixed point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in E_n
              in that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(e,g) = e
              are the neutral elements.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p The canonical action
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G \times G \to G
            %p of any simplicial group on itself is principal.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (simplicial principal bundle)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a simplicial group, a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
              of
              = succeed "es" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is called a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %strong simplicial principal bundle
              if
            %ul
              %li
                %p the action is principal;
              %li
                %p
                  the base is isomorphic to the quotient
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi G
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ×
                        %mi G
                        %mover
                          %mrow
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 1
                            %mi E
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E/G := \lim_{\to}(E \times G \stackrel{\overset{\rho}{\to}}{\underset{p_1}{\to} E})
                  by the action:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi G
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi X
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        E/G \simeq X
                        \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              A simplicial
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
              is necessarly a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              This appears as Lemma 18.2 in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#MaySimplicialObjects"} MaySimpOb
          %h4#UniversalSimplicialBundle
            Universal simplicial
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a simplicial group, define the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G
              to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decalage"} decalage
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{W}G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Dec
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W G := Dec \overline{W}G
                    \\,.
          %p
            By the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            this means that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
            any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mo •
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                          %mi G
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mo •
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi W
                            %mo ¯
                          %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P_\bullet &amp;\to&amp; W G
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X_\bullet &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; \overline{W}G
                  }
          %p
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            exhibits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_\bullet
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mo •
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mo •
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi W
                            %mo ¯
                          %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P_\bullet &amp;\to&amp; *
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X_\bullet &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; \overline{W}G
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            i.e. as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            of the cocycle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              We call
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mo •
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mo ×
                      %mi g
                    %mi W
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_\bullet := X_\bullet \times^g W G
              the simplicial
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
              corresponding to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\phi : X_n \to G_{(n-1)}\}
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisting+function"} twisting function
              corresponding to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : X_\bullet \to \overline{W}G
              by the above discussion.
            %p
              Then the simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mo •
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi g
                    %mi W
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_\bullet := X_\bullet \times_{g} W G
              is explicitly given by the formula called the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cartesian+product"} twisted Cartesian product
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                      %msup
                        %mo ×
                        %mi ϕ
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \times^\phi G_\bullet
            %p its cells are
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    P_n  = X_n \times G_n
            %p with face and degeneracy maps
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi i
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi i
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_i (x,g) = (d_i x , d_i g)
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \gt 0
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 0
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 0
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0 (x,g) = (d_0 x, \phi(x) d_0 g)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi i
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi i
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_i (x,g) = (s_i x, s_i g)
                  \.
          %h4#SimplicialBundleReferences References
          %p Here are some pointers on where precisely in the literature the above statements can be found.
          %p One useful reference is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
              ,
              %em Simplicial Objects in Algebraic Topology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/Simp.djvu"}> djvu
              ).
          %p
            There the abbreviation PCTP (
            %em principal twisted cartesian product
            ) is used for what above we called just
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cartesian+product"} twisted Cartesian product
          %p
            The fact that every PTCP
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times_\phi G \to X
            defined by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisting+function"} twisting function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            arises as the pullback of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo ¯
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G \to \overline{W}G
            along a morphism of simplicial sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo ¯
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \overline{W}G
            can be found there by combining
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the last sentence on p. 81 which asserts that pullbacks of PTCPs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi ϕ
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times_\phi G \to X
                along morphisms of simplicial sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
                yield PTCPs corresponding to the composite of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                with
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            %li
              %p
                section 21 which establishes that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G \to \bar W G
                is the PTCP for some universal twisting function
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r(G)
            %li
              %p
                lemma 21.9 states in the language of composites of twisting functions that every PTCP comes from composing a cocycle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to \bar W G
                with the universal twisting function
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r(G)
          %p
            An explicit version of the statement that
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cartesian+product"} twisted Cartesian product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
            is on
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/timporter/files/menagerie10.pdf#page=148"} page 148
            of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"}> Tim Porter
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/timporter/show/crossed+menagerie"}> The Crossed Menagerie
                \.
          %p
            On
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/timporter/files/menagerie10.pdf#page=239"} page 239
            there it is mentioned that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo ¯
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G \to W G \to \overline{W}G
          %p
            is a model for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G \to * \to \mathbf{B}G
                  \\,.
          %p
            One place in the literature where the observation that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decalage"} decalage
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo ¯
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{W}G
            is mentioned fairly explicitly is page 85 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Duskin"}> John Duskin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Simplicial methods and the interpretation of “triple” cohomology
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group+action"} simplicial group action
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+topological+group"} simplicial topological group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} group object in an (∞,1)-category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"}> 2-group
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+crossed+module"} differential crossed module
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-group"}> 3-group
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-crossed+module"} 2-crossed module
                \/
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+square"} crossed square
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+2-crossed+module"} differential 2-crossed module
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-group"} n-group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"}> ∞-group
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong simplicial group
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercrossed+complex"} hypercrossed complex
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+groups"} model structure on simplicial groups
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+model+structure"} Borel model structure
          %h2#references_2 References
          %ul
            %li#Quillen67
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
                , II §3.8 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopical+Algebra"} Homotopical Algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 43
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0097438"} doi:10.1007/BFb0097438
            %li#MaySimplicialObjects
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
                , Chapter IV, Section 17 of:
                %em Simplicial Objects in Algebraic Topology
                University of Chicago Press 1967 (
                %a{:href => "https://press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/S/bo5956688.html"}> ISBN:9780226511818
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/Simp.djvu"} djvu
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/May_SimplicialObjectsInAlgebraicTopology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Curtis71
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+B.+Curtis"}> Edward B. Curtis
                , Section 3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Simplicial homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0001-8708(71)90015-6"} doi:10.1016/0001-8708(71)90015-6
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=279808"} MR279808
            %li#GoerssJardine
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"} J. F. Jardine
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simplicial+homotopy+theory"} Simplicial homotopy theory
                Progress in Mathematics, Birkhäuser (1999), Modern Birkhäuser Classics (2009) (
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://web.archive.org/web/19990208220238/http://www.math.uwo.ca/~jardine/papers/simp-sets/"} webpage
            %li#Weibel94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Weibel"}> Charles Weibel
                , Chapter 8 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An introduction to homological algebra
          %p The algorithm for finding the horn fillers in a simplicial group is given in the proof of theorem 17.1, page 67 there.
          %p This proof that simplicial groups are Kan complexes is originally due to Moore, see theorem 3.4 in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Moore"}> John Moore
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Semi-Simplicial Complexes And Postnikov Systems
              %em Symposium International De Topologia Algebraica
              , 1956 conference, book published in 1958
          %p which earlier appeared in more detail as Theorem 3 on p. 18-04 of
          %ul
            %li#Moore54
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Moore"}> John Moore
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopie des complexes monoideaux, I
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=SHC_1954-1955__7_2_A8_0"} numdam:SHC_1954-1955__7_2_A8_0
          %p and is often referenced to
          %ul
            %li#Moore
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Moore"}> John Moore
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic homotopy theory
          %p
            In fact, it seems that this is the origin of the very notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          %p A proof is also on p. 14 of
          %ul
            %li#JoyalTierney05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Myles+Tierney"} Myles Tierney
              chapter I of
              = succeed "," do
                %em An introduction to simplicial homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
